    tests cover the header, newest-first default order, both sorts in both directions, the filter keeping the sort (and
    the reverse), the four chip colors, durations, the empty states and the fallback for bad query values.
  - [1mTask 2:[0m the [38;5;153m/deploys[39m route, the "Deploys" nav link after "Services", a route test and a 503 test, two test data
    files, and a README line.

  [1mThings worth knowing[0m
  - [1mIt uses the existing component kit.[0m [38;5;153mvendor/kit[39m (imported as [38;5;153m#kit/*[39m) already has [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m, [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m + [38;5;153mselectField[39m,
    [38;5;153mdataTable[39m (sortable headers included), [38;5;153mbadge[39m and [38;5;153memptyState[39m. So the page is built from those rather than copying
    the hand-written table and [38;5;153m<select>[39m from [38;5;153mservices.js[39m. It behaves the same as Services; only the markup classes
    differ ([38;5;153mkit-table[39m and [38;5;153mkit-badge[39m instead of [38;5;153mservices[39m and [38;5;153mpill[39m). The status colors map onto the kit's tones: succeeded
    → [38;5;153mok[39m (green), failed → [38;5;153mbad[39m (red), rolled-back → [38;5;153mwarn[39m (amber), in-progress → [38;5;153minfo[39m (blue).
  - [1mTask 2 has to add test data files.[0m The e2e tests open every nav link against [38;5;153mtest/e2e/fixtures/empty/[39m and [38;5;153msingle/[39m,
    and neither folder has a [38;5;153mdeploys.json[39m. Adding the nav link alone would make those tests fail with 503s, so Task 2
    adds both files.

  [1mThree choices the spec doesn't cover[0m
